---
description: Create a git commit
---

Create a git commit with all current changes. First run `git status` and `git diff --staged` to review the current state. Stage all relevant changes. Write a clear, concise commit message following a conventional Commits format. If there is a CONTRIBUTING.md or similar docs specifying commit conventions, follow those instead. Run `git diff --staged` once more to confirm the staging area looks correct, then commit. Finally, push to the appropriate remote (e.g. `git push origin main`). If the remote or branch is ambiguous, ask which remote/branch to push to.
